{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ec97a360612395b0","name":"card_unit_cyclone_division","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BloodIron/units/card_unit_cyclone_division","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CYCLONE DIVISION","text":"Deployment: Add a Sherman to hand. Becomes Veteran when you have deployed 2 Shermans.","flavorText":"The 38th Infantry Division, known as the Cyclone Division, is a US Army division which was first formed in 1917, served in WWI, and in the Pacific Theater during WWII. The division earned its nickname due to the cyclone emblem on its insignia, symbolizing its force and resilience. After extensive jungle and amphibious warfare training, the Cyclone Division saw major combat during the Philippines Campaign. Its notable actions include intense fighting on Luzon in early 1945, where it played a critical role in pushing back entrenched Japanese forces. One of its most famous achievements was its involvement in liberating Bataan and Corregidor, earning it the title “Avengers of Bataan” in recognition of its success in reclaiming ground previously lost to Japanese forces in 1942. On 15 September 1945 the division returned to the United States and was demobilized.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":6,"operationCost":3,"attack":7,"defense":7},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_cyclone_division","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_cyclone_division_title","SourceString":"CYCLONE DIVISION","LocalizedString":"CYCLONE DIVISION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":7,"defense":7,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_cyclone_division_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Add a Sherman to hand. Becomes Veteran when you have deployed 2 Shermans.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Add a Sherman to hand. Becomes Veteran when you have deployed 2 Shermans."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_cyclone_division_history","SourceString":"The 38th Infantry Division, known as the Cyclone Division, is a US Army division which was first formed in 1917, served in WWI, and in the Pacific Theater during WWII. The division earned its nickname due to the cyclone emblem on its insignia, symbolizing its force and resilience. After extensive jungle and amphibious warfare training, the Cyclone Division saw major combat during the Philippines Campaign. Its notable actions include intense fighting on Luzon in early 1945, where it played a critical role in pushing back entrenched Japanese forces. One of its most famous achievements was its involvement in liberating Bataan and Corregidor, earning it the title “Avengers of Bataan” in recognition of its success in reclaiming ground previously lost to Japanese forces in 1942. On 15 September 1945 the division returned to the United States and was demobilized.","LocalizedString":"The 38th Infantry Division, known as the Cyclone Division, is a US Army division which was first formed in 1917, served in WWI, and in the Pacific Theater during WWII. The division earned its nickname due to the cyclone emblem on its insignia, symbolizing its force and resilience. After extensive jungle and amphibious warfare training, the Cyclone Division saw major combat during the Philippines Campaign. Its notable actions include intense fighting on Luzon in early 1945, where it played a critical role in pushing back entrenched Japanese forces. One of its most famous achievements was its involvement in liberating Bataan and Corregidor, earning it the title “Avengers of Bataan” in recognition of its success in reclaiming ground previously lost to Japanese forces in 1942. On 15 September 1945 the division returned to the United States and was demobilized."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","isInPermanentPool":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFr